## Overview

This project develops a proof-of-concept workflow for assessing how human mobility can modify environmental exposure estimates in the Helsinki metropolitan area.

The analysis progresses from conventional residential exposure toward mobility-based exposure.

## Analytical framework

### 1. Residential exposure

PM₂.₅ concentrations are assigned to populated grid cells to characterize environmental conditions at residential locations.

[View the residential exposure analysis](notebooks/01_residential_pm25_exposure.ipynb)

### 2. Mobility-weighted destination exposure

Origin-destination mobility flows are combined with neighbourhood-level PM₂.₅ concentrations to examine whether mobility takes residents toward relatively cleaner or more polluted environments.

[View the mobility exposure analysis](notebooks/02_mobility_weighted_destination_exposure.ipynb)

### 3. Route-based exposure

Candidate walking routes are reconstructed using OpenStreetMap. PM₂.₅ concentrations are sampled along each route and combined with estimated travel time to construct a concentration-time exposure indicator.

[View the route exposure analysis](notebooks/03_candidate_walking_route_pm25_exposure.ipynb)

